{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Ticket 2 (uncheering-uncivil-pig, DET-tier priority backfill): TDD held-out loop -- no separate edge/E2E cases exist for this leaf (pure constant addition, single behavior per site), so both RED oracles (test_code_review_ws5.py::test_failclosed_forces_block_on_detector_match, test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py::test_oversized_bug_fix_without_attestation_blocks) were the full happy-path spec, confirmed RED (KeyError: priority) before dispatch. Implementer subagent (1 attempt) added exactly `priority: 1.0`/`0.9` alongside unchanged severity/decision (expand-contract, per the plan-review-caught coupling with shim.py). Validated: both targeted tests + full 72-test files green; mutation-teeth check run inside a macOS sandbox-exec profile (scoped to worktree + scratch dir) -- perturbing priority to 0.5 drove the detectors.py test RED for the right reason, then restored (had to redo the restore outside the sandbox since git's worktree index.lock lives outside the sandboxed subpath -- accidentally discarded the uncommitted fix via `git checkout --` and had to re-apply the single line). Refactoring litmus: trivial pass (tests assert finding-dict values, not internal structure). Lint/format/mypy on touched files: clean. Full `make test` (pytest -m \"not integration and not external\") took unusually long (>45min, still running as task bvvtb8mcf) -- given the change's low risk (pure data addition, fully covered by the 72 targeted tests) and that CI's Verified gate runs the same suite, proceeded to commit+push rather than block on it. Pushed to Gerrit: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2445. Also plan-review caught two real defects in my ticket authoring before this landed: (1) my original AC wrongly claimed `decision` needed to be ADDED when it already existed at both sites; (2) my \"delete severity\" AC would have broken shim.py's severity->common-severity mapping (silent downgrade to `medium`) since shim.py's own migration (ticket 3, beaming-snively-urial) hasn't landed yet -- fixed by switching ticket 2 to expand-contract (add priority, keep severity; severity removal deferred to the final cleanup ticket)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788124564793137126,"uuid":"9db45250-ab85-4c3b-9744-d8873f64c06b"}